Description: pvr: keep device tile buffers on vkCmdBeginRendering errors
 The tile buffers in device->tile_buffer_state are shared by all render
 states and command buffers of the device and only grow
 (pvr_device_tile_buffer_ensure_cap()). The error path of
 vkCmdBeginRendering() after a failed render state setup or sub command start
 called pvr_device_free_tile_buffer_state(), which frees every tile buffer but
 leaves buffer_count and the pointers unchanged. Command buffers that were
 recorded or are pending keep the GPU addresses of the freed buffers, later
 recordings read the freed pvr_bo structures (pvr_arch_cmd_buffer.c, tile
 buffer addresses from device->tile_buffer_state),
 pvr_device_tile_buffer_ensure_cap() does not replace them, and device
 destruction frees them a second time.
 .
 Leave the tile buffers alone on these errors; they are released with the
 device as before.
 .
 Only for this downstream stack; not intended for upstream submission.
Author: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Generated-by: LLM
Forwarded: not-needed

